  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000005991</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring equal rights for women and girls by reforming the Muslim Marriage and Divorce Act (MMDA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to create awareness and clarity amongst, mostly Muslim young men and community leaders, of the need to fully reform the MMDA and to muster support from the Muslim community to publicly impress upon the need to substantially reform the law and the reformed MMDA to be administered by better and an accountable justice system. It also wanted to empower the affected women to demand a full reform of the law and the current unequal administrative structure. Reforming                                                                                                                                   t he MMDA to remove the discriminatory provisions and aspects that discriminate Muslim women and girl children and bring this personal law in conformity with the equality provisions guaranteed as fundamental rights in the constitution thus ensuring the retention of the personal laws that reflect diversity.</narrative>
  </description>
